y":[]},{"date":"2021-03-16T18:03:48-07:00","id":1440308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1440300#post1440300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While table top games follow coteries, a TV show would be better suited to switching between a range of characters and settings</div> </div> </div> </div>A World of Darkness TV show would suffer greatly from an Outer Limits-style show. It would need to really have a coherent ongoing plot and specific cast of characters, in order to maintain the interest of normal viewership, especially if you do any kind of depth of lore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1808,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","user":"elmerg","date":". 03-16-2021, 09:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-16T18:28:30-07:00","id":1440315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1440308#post1440308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A World of Darkness TV show would suffer greatly from an Outer Limits-style show. It would need to really have a coherent ongoing plot and specific cast of characters, in order to maintain the interest of normal viewership, especially if you do any kind of depth of lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>On Netflix there's a SPECTACULARLY terrible show called Immortals that is obviously just someone's Turkish Vampire: The Masquerade game.<br /> <br /> It was great to watch, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-16T19:47:23-07:00","id":1440320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1440308#post1440308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A World of Darkness TV show would suffer greatly from an Outer Limits-style show. It would need to really have a coherent ongoing plot and specific cast of characters, in order to maintain the interest of normal viewership, especially if you do any kind of depth of lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>My use of the word &quot;settings&quot; may have been misleading. I mean that it shouldn't just focus on a group of 25 year old Anarchs, but that the main characters should be spread across several elements of kindred society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","user":"Spencer from The Hills","date":". 03-16-2021, 10:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-17T02:27:01-07:00","id":1440345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1440315#post1440315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On Netflix there's a SPECTACULARLY terrible show called Immortals that is obviously just someone's Turkish Vampire: The Masquerade game.<br /> <br /> It was great to watch, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>100% agree, though the concept of a wooden karambit still makes my head hurt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-17T02:38:26-07:00","id":1440346,"title":"","content":"If we really want to mess with peoples minds with a V:tM show, have it set at a college town where the local LARP group plays. The protagonist of the story is brought into the LARP and over time begins to lose touch with what is reality and what is game, only to find out at the end of the first season they were actually ghouled by a Malkavian during the LARP.<br /> <br /> Dementation doesn't require SFX, nor does the Malkavian clan weakness. Obfuscate can be covered by camera tricks and forced perspective. Auspex most of the time can be covered by exposition, with only the higher levels requiring SFX. The only problem is that the mental health advocates will get cranky if the weakness isn't handled carefully.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-17T03:32:13-07:00","id":1440350,"title":"","content":"Honestly, what's interesting is the fact that we DO have V:TM shows. It's just the ultra-cheap LivePlays that pretty much are plotted out seasons of television.<br /> <br /> Victor Temple and Annabelle are pretty much showing how a V:TM show would go with a budget.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-17T06:30:11-07:00","id":1440353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1440346#post1440346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we really want to mess with peoples minds with a V:tM show, have it set at a college town where the local LARP group plays. The protagonist of the story is brought into the LARP and over time begins to lose touch with what is reality and what is game, only to find out at the end of the first season they were actually ghouled by a Malkavian during the LARP.</div> </div> </div> </div> If you want to forever deny the possibility of becoming mainstream, show off LARP. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dementation doesn't require SFX, nor does the Malkavian clan weakness. Obfuscate can be covered by camera tricks and forced perspective. . </div> </div> </div>Unless you're heavily abusing Potence or Celerity, none of the common disciplines (not counting Protean) require SFX, and Obtenebration/Chimestry/Diamonion can be really cheap. Celerity, unless you have something to contrast it to, should be really easy to do; just speed things up. <br /> WoD isn't the kind of setting where you put glowing lights and blur effects on everything magic. Magic is as subtle as it can be. It follows the path of least resistance. The stuff vampires need is generally pretty cheap. Only Vicissitude and Protean really require good money thrown at them, and even then... you can get around a lot of that by skipping the transformations themselves; a mist machine won't break the bank. Now Werewolf, on the otherhand.... yeesh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-17T09:13:38-07:00","id":1440362,"title":"","content":"If Netflix could pull off a V:tM show along the same production value and writing quality lines of Daredevil or Jessica Jones, it would probably do very well. Vampires, intrigue, smart writing and decent effects would draw in the average viewer, while the any nods to the TTRPG or Bloodlines would be appreciated by regular fans.<br /> <br /> Using the Volume tech from <i>Mandalorian</i> would allow for a vampire show with mostly scenes at night, rather then necessitating lame \u201cday walker\u201d excuses for shooting schedule, like with <i>Embraced</i> and <i>Diaries</i>.<br /> <br /> Hell, we could probably get two good seasons before Netflix cancels it out of the blue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-17T10:29:42-07:00","id":1440363,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m going to buck the trend a bit and say if you really want to build a World of Darkness shared universe akin to the MCU... don\u2019t START with Vampire; start with Mage.<br /> <br /> Mages, particularly newly Awakened ones are, bare none, the closest to mortals in abilities and perspective to normal humans of any of the main WoD splats. That makes them ideal for an opening viewpoint character and subtle fx requirements to start.<br /> <br /> But also important is that a big part of Mage is that everything man has ever believed in exists in somewhere in the shadows. This preps the stage for the larger universe with meeting vampires, werewolves, wraiths, changelings, etc. before spinning off an associated series where we get more details on the specific supernatural type.<br /> <br /> I also really think VtM on its own just doesn\u2019t have enough unique on its own to make it a viable IP for a Netflix style series. But the larger WoD as a shared universe IS fairly unique (and rarely as well put together; ex. the Vampire Diaries and its spin-offs).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-17T11:39:27-07:00","id":1440368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1440363#post1440363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m going to buck the trend a bit and say if you really want to build a World of Darkness shared universe akin to the MCU... don\u2019t START with Vampire; start with Mage.<br /> <br /> Mages, particularly newly Awakened ones are, bare none, the closest to mortals in abilities and perspective to normal humans of any of the main WoD splats. That makes them ideal for an opening viewpoint character and subtle fx requirements to start.<br /> <br /> But also important is that a big part of Mage is that everything man has ever believed in exists in somewhere in the shadows. This preps the stage for the larger universe with meeting vampires, werewolves, wraiths, changelings, etc. before spinning off an associated series where we get more details on the specific supernatural type.<br /> <br /> I also really think VtM on its own just doesn\u2019t have enough unique on its own to make it a viable IP for a Netflix style series. But the larger WoD as a shared universe IS fairly unique (and rarely as well put together; ex. the Vampire Diaries and its spin-offs).</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to disagree for multiple reasons:<br /> <br /> 1. Vampire is simply more popular.<br /> <br /> 2. Vampire is also something proven to already have a very adaptable premise given things like Blade: The Series, Underworld, True Blood, and other stories about &quot;vampire mafias.&quot;<br /> <br /> 3. Mage is probably the hardest to actually explain. It is a VERY esoteric game in terms of factions and ideas.<br /> <br /> 4. As for not being &quot;unique&quot; enough, you're not selling the premise anyway. You're selling the content. What will make a V:TM game would be acting and characters.<br /> <br /> But that's just me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-17T12:05:45-07:00","id":1440371,"title":"","content":"Obviously, one must start with Hunter. <br /> -Easiest to explain. <br /> -Domestic terrorism is fun for the whole family. <br /> -No factions necessary. <br /> -Main character learns as audience does. <br /> you can dive into vampire from there. <br /> -That bottom-up approach to the setting is just a good way of getting people into the zone. Just trying to explain mage politics is offputting, you just can't lead with it. Especially as, in mage, the interplay between all these different factions is important and you can't just use the Order of Hermes without... houses and technoxrats and other traditions and oh my. Vampire, at least, is largely just -the Camarilla- and you can sideline everything else till you want to use them. Hunters are perfect because you just have Robert and Jane trying to avenge their dead kids and they themselves don't even know about the SoL.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-17T12:47:25-07:00","id":1440376,"title":"","content":"[ETA] This is in reply to CTPhipps last post, I just didn\u2019t feel like including a long quote block when his points were numbered for easy replies... [/ETA]<br /> <br /> You and I completely disagree on something? This is my shocked face... -_-<br /> <br /> 1) Let\u2019s be honest here, neither property is setting the world on fire at the moment. Compared to Blade or Dr. Strange they\u2019re both F-tier IPs at best.<br /> <br /> 2) The fact that you can mention so many properties that have already done what VtM does and are vastly more present in the public consciousness is all the more reason to NOT make VtM your tentpole property for a larger World of Darkness media universe.<br /> <br /> 3) Elevator-Pitch Explanation: Mages are people who can push reality to align with their wills, but suffer pushback called paradox if they push it too far out of line. Mages with similar desires band together into traditions that are in conflict with each other over the direction to push the world.<br /> <br /> 3a) Most people have read/watched Harry Potter... a hidden magical world existing alongside the mundane one isn\u2019t something that needs lengthy explanations these days; just the nature of the factions, their goals and how each works their magic.<br /> <br /> 3b) Most mages don\u2019t understand how magic works at the metaphysics-level; each tradition has its own beliefs, practices and props and viewers only need be introduced to those one at a time. In keeping with 3a I\u2019d personally open with an orphan who is found by a member of House Ex Miscellanea who\u2019s Hermetic paradigm is close enough to what many consider \u201cdefault wizardry\u201d that it doesn\u2019t need much explanation. Then you can start introducing people who do things differently.<br /> <br /> 4) Just what content do you think is so unique you couldn\u2019t just skip the virtually unheard of outside of RPG circles IPs and write your own vampire story where the lore can be exactly what you want instead of paying money so that superfans can incessantly bitch at you that you\u2019re adapting it wrong?<br /> <br /> That last one is 1000% why this will never happen. Anything you\u2019d want to do with VtM could just as easily be written in a generic urban fantasy universe with some of the names filed off for less money, less superfan backlash and less interference from the rights holders.<br /> <br /> Using VtM as the basis for a series is a Lose/Lose proposition. Frankly, so is Mage, it\u2019s just slightly less so because it wouldn\u2019t feel quite as derivative as VtM would look after decades of vampire shows and movies ripping off all the best ideas from it (it doesn\u2019t matter if VtM did it first, it matters that they\u2019ve already seen it if they\u2019ve watched any vampire-themes genre series in the last 20 years). At least Mage has the potential to expand past looking like a Harry Potter rip-off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1328,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","user":"Chris24601","date":". 03-17-2021, 03:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-17T12:47:53-07:00","id":1440377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1440371#post1440371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously, one must start with Hunter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always found it funny that Hunter got three video games despite being one of the lower tier recognizable lines.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-17T13:02:10-07:00","id":1440381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1440377#post1440377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I always found it funny that Hunter got three video games despite being one of the lower tier recognizable lines.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's the most intuitive. <br /> <br /> Compare<br /> So you undertook your first change during puberty, becoming a werewolf killing machine of power, now you have ran away from home to join a cult and work with the spirit world to save the planet with your pack...<br /> To<br /> Kill the vampires hiding in society. <br /> <br /> High-concept wise, it's the easiest sell by far. No need to look like a dork at your pitch meeting explaining the intricacies of Tradition politics and the metaphysics of paradox, and no need to water down your product to make it more palatable to the &quot;her name is khalessi&quot; crowd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-17T14:25:29-07:00","id":1440385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1440377#post1440377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always found it funny that Hunter got three video games despite being one of the lower tier recognizable lines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Always remember, if it\u2019s not D&amp;D then EVERY rpg game line is the lowest tier of recognizable outside of rpg circles. Hell, I know non-rper who use \u201cD&amp;D\u201d as synonymous with \u201crpg\u201d as in \u201cWhat sort of D&amp;D are you guys playing?\u201d<br /> <br /> In terms of percentage of the general population the difference in numbers between those who\u2019ve heard of VtM vs. Hunter is in the fractions of a percent (remember 3.5 million copies of something wouldn\u2019t even be 1% of the US population or 0.05% of the global population).<br /> <br /> Bloodlines sold less than 100,000 copies. The pilot episode of The Vampire Diaries had 4.93 million viewers and even its lowest rated episodes in its eighth season had 10 times the viewers as Bloodlines sold copies. Twilight made $407 million in theatres and sold over 11 million DVDs.<br /> <br /> In short, the difference in popularity between VtM and HtR outside of role-playing circles is a rounding error. As such, I\u2019ll agree in a general sense with Hunter being the logical starting point with the caveat that \u201cHunters Hunted\u201d Hunters are an even more sensible start point.<br /> <br /> That said, HtR and HH have exactly the same problems as the rest of the World of Darkness... there\u2019s just not enough unique to it to make the IP worth acquiring over just having some already famous screenwriter bang out an urban fantasy script.<br /> <br /> Even the IP names are too damned generic. Take the maybe 10% of the content you\u2019d actually want to use in season one, file off the names (they\u2019re not Nosferatu, they\u2019re Orlocks... they\u2019re not Tremere they\u2019re the House Dracul*), add one or two elements from elsewhere, and call the whole thing \u201cVampires.\u201d You wouldn\u2019t have to pay White Wolf a dime and any claim of infringement would be laughted out of court.<br /> <br /> * This plays on the original novel\u2019s lore that Dracula gained his many supernatural powers from a Satanic academy of magic... drinking blood was just the Satanic price for immortality. Take it a step further and replace the Caine/Antediluvian origin with various figures throughout history who reputably sold their souls to the Devil for supernatural power (so a bloodline of Rasputin, a bloodline of Caligula, etc.) becoming the first vampire of each \u201clineage\u201d and because each bargain was a little different, each lineage has different strengths and weaknesses.<br /> <br /> Inventing new vampire lore is stupid-easy at this point; there\u2019s zero reason to pay the owners of VtM for theirs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-17T17:25:03-07:00","id":1440398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1440058#post1440058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you tried the V:TM comic?</div> </div> </div> </div>It wasn't bad. The art is good and including the characters and background as loresheets and with stats was definitely a great idea. The main characters were ok, just that. Though I read up to #5 (I think it's the last one) the story didn't interest me that much, neither did the other characters, specially the thin-blood/anarch secondary story. Thing is, I'm not interested in more characters when the canon story already have a lot of them.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-17T20:03:02-07:00","id":1440404,"title":"","content":"The single biggest obstacle to a Vampire: The Masquerade tv series is probably the &quot;Elric Problem&quot;. <br /> <br /> For those that have never heard of it, Elric of Melnibone is Michael Moorcock's dark fantasy albino swordsman who has been around since the early 1960s, and one of his nicknames, &quot;The White Wolf&quot;, was the inspiration for the White Wolf Games Studios' name. There was recently an effort to get an Elric streaming series made. The problem was that everyone who looked at it said it was too much like The Witcher. The Witcher franchise, which started in the 90s, very clearly derives a lot of its influences from Elric. <br /> Vampire has a similar issue, in that ever since the first Blade movie very clearly &quot;borrowed&quot; a lot of ideas from it, too many other things look like Vampire, especially to the intellectually challenged individuals who run most entertainment studios. With Disney+ already having announced an MCU Blade streaming series (or film, I forget which), and the existence of things like the Underworld franchise, which more Hollywood type people are likely to have heard of, trying to sell them on a V:tM series would probably be an uphill battle. <br /> The likely exception is if you tried to sell them on turning LA by Night into a streaming fiction series. They might bite at that. (NPI)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-17T20:06:05-07:00","id":1440405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1440404#post1440404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The single biggest obstacle to a Vampire: The Masquerade tv series is probably the &quot;Elric Problem&quot;.<br /> <br /> For those that have never heard of it, Elric of Melnibone is Michael Moorcock's dark fantasy albino swordsman who has been around since the early 1960s, and one of his nicknames, &quot;The White Wolf&quot;, was the inspiration for the White Wolf Games Studios' name. There was recently an effort to get an Elric streaming series made. The problem was that everyone who looked at it said it was too much like The Witcher. The Witcher franchise, which started in the 90s, very clearly derives a lot of its influences from Elric.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hilarious fact, Michael Moorcock tried to start a plagarism war over Elric and Geralt's connection.<br /> <br /> Sapkowski went, &quot;Oh yeah, I was definitely inspired by Elric in a lot of what I did. Fantastic books. Lots of homages.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which sort of sucked the wind out of Michael's sales.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1440398#post1440398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It wasn't bad. The art is good and including the characters and background as loresheets and with stats was definitely a great idea. The main characters were ok, just that. Though I read up to #5 (I think it's the last one) the story didn't interest me that much, neither did the other characters, specially the thin-blood/anarch secondary story. Thing is, I'm not interested in more characters when the canon story already have a lot of them.<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>I really enjoy the books and they basically give me an idea of how you would do the show, IMHO. You'd have a central point of view vampire, one city, and a cast slowly developed with things like Anarchs as well as Camarilla being introduced as a result. I kind of regret the comic book isn't getting more attention. I also think its kind of funny that its being made by an infamous cheesecake artist and gore hound (Tim Seeley) by is actually really tame even by industry standards.<br /> <br /> Probably a good thing but surprising.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-17-2021, 11:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-17T20:18:35-07:00","id":1440406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1440081#post1440081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be honest I am not much of a comics person. Most comics out there are put together to keep readers reading, rather than to tell a specific story which has an ending.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the difference between serial comics and graphic novels (V for Vendetta, Watchmen, From Hell, Maus, The Harlem Hellfighters, Boxers &amp; Saints, Dark Knight: A True Batman Story, I Kill Giants, A History of Violence). Sort of like the difference between a daily soap opera and a film or miniseries. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T01:05:04-07:00","id":1440424,"title":"","content":"Fun fact: I used to email Michael Moorcock on and off when I ran a SF/F magazine. He's a good guy.<br /> <br /> I think you can start with a newly Embraced character in the opening episode, but you're not tied to only following that person. I would have the first episode be their introduction to the World of Darkness, and it ends when they first set foot in Elysium or something. Then, the next episode picks up at that point and lets us slowly zoom out, meeting more and more of the vampires in this world, and uncovering the intricate machinations going on behind the scenes.<br /> <br /> I think it can be done. The Elric problem is real, but not insurmountable. The other way to pitch Elric would've been 'a rival to The Witcher for our network, but based on a pre-existing work so without worry about getting sued'.<br /> <br /> DC and Marvel have various superheroes who are superficially similar to each other, but that doesn't stop them exploiting those characters. You just need to see this as an opportunity rather than a barrier.<br /> <br /> A show that could mop up viewers of Blade, Vampire Diaries, True Blood, Underworld, etc, isn't a bad thing. Often, the same people watch those shows anyway. If you like vampires, you like vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 03-19-2021, 10:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T18:25:39-07:00","id":1440528,"title":"","content":"Hmm. I think if I were to try to make a Vampire series - let's say a Netflix style streaming one with 10 episodes - I would probably have it mainly focus on a Sire and Childe as the two main characters, with their interaction being the backbone, and their interactions with others branching off from there. Not sure which Clan, but most likely Brujah or Ventrue. They'd be a window into the worlds of Elders and Neonates, respectively. They aren't enemies, but aren't exactly bosom companions either. Their relationship should be complicated and multifaceted, with more than a few parallels and/or reflections in their stories. <br /> I'm not really sure which city would work best as a setting. While LA and Chicago would certainly be interesting, I think New York might be the most optimal choice due to size, age, and density. <br /> The Elder story would likely involve two or three other characters, having ties to each other going back to the 19th century or earlier. This is a very complex game, usually with very subtle moves and deep plots. <br /> The Neonate story is maybe three or four other characters, with more of a focus on the nightlife of the Rack, interpersonal relationships among vampires who are still young enough to still be thinking a lot like the humans they were in life. Possibly at least one trying to be in a relationship with a living mortal. <br /> The season (or series, if only a one and done) finale would have some sort of significant alteration in the Sire and Childe's relationship that has been built to over the season. Also probably the death (or apparent death) of at least one supporting character. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T05:40:49-07:00","id":1440581,"title":"","content":"Whoa this thread blew up <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Lots of good arguments there why we haven't seen a V:TM show yet on Netflix/Amazon. The average viewer probably doesn't understand the difference between V:tM and say V Wars. It's all the same to them. But it's hard to believe that theres no producer who played V:tM in his youth and doesn't think &quot;hey, if we do a vampire series, why not do it with all the lore that is part of WoD?&quot; I mean things like &quot;American Gods&quot; get 3+ seasons and they are totally confusing to the average viewer i assume - and its totally shallow in comparison and wouldnt need any god involvement whatsoever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23838-marcus-meridian","name":"Marcus Meridian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23838_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T07:33:16-07:00","id":1440593,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I think VTM sets itself apart from the copy pastes with one simple reason:<br /> It's a parody of the real world. <br /> The Ventrue isn't prunning on a throne, he's managing financial and political assets. <br /> The Toreador isn't just there for gossip and holding elysium, she's helping people avoid paying taxes through charity and fine art. Or maybe she's using her influence to fuck with financial markets. <br /> The Brujah just <i>is </i>the unions. <br /> The Lasombra are playing corporate raider.<br /> The Tremere are just... a company. <br /> <br /> So many shows give us sleek, sexy vampires who seemingly have all the money because they had treasure 500 years ago and the valuation on that is way too high. Vampire gives us stories about accounting and embezzelment and trying to justify why there's four dead bodies whilst also mitigating wrath of a Toreador because you said the wrong thing at her party. WoD vampires are just so... ugly, and it's great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T09:47:44-07:00","id":1440611,"title":"","content":"To make a WoD series stand out, it would require writers who understand the difference between episodic tv where everything more or less resets between episodes, and a consequence driven universe. The slightest whiff of &quot;plot armor&quot; and the series is sunk, in fact to keep proper pace with how bad the WoD setting and characters are, you could make an argument that it might almost need to go &quot;grim dark&quot; or at the very least have the writers chant the mantra that all characters are wearing &quot;plot bomb vests&quot; rather than &quot;plot armor&quot;. Basically the characters have to be smart to survive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T15:42:25-07:00","id":1440653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1440611#post1440611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To make a WoD series stand out, it would require writers who understand the difference between episodic tv where everything more or less resets between episodes, and a consequence driven universe. The slightest whiff of &quot;plot armor&quot; and the series is sunk, in fact to keep proper pace with how bad the WoD setting and characters are, you could make an argument that it might almost need to go &quot;grim dark&quot; or at the very least have the writers chant the mantra that all characters are wearing &quot;plot bomb vests&quot; rather than &quot;plot armor&quot;. Basically the characters have to be smart to survive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see why there's any desire to make Vampire: The Masquerade less plot armory than other series. What attracts people to the story is not the threat of death to the main characters but the romanticism and mystique of the undead as well as their complicated politics.<br /> <br /> A vampire will survive 900 things that would kill a human protagonist so one would think that WOD characters would have a lot MORE plot armor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T07:50:13-07:00","id":1440718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1440653#post1440653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see why there's any desire to make Vampire: The Masquerade less plot armory than other series. What attracts people to the story is not the threat of death to the main characters but the romanticism and mystique of the undead as well as their complicated politics.<br /> <br /> A vampire will survive 900 things that would kill a human protagonist so one would think that WOD characters would have a lot MORE plot armor.</div> </div> </div> </div>The threat of death isn't for the viewers, it's for the writers.<br /> <br /> If you really think about a storyline and realize that the protagonist could have stayed home and the antagonist, if left to their own devices, have defeated themselves, the audience is going to call BS. You can't have an appreciation for the politics in vampire if they make no sense or have no value as written.<br /> <br /> Most vampire politics are written in reverse order. Basically a writer wants a specific story to happen so they reverse engineer some politics to push the characters in a given direction. When doing world building, especially in an detail oriented book or tv series, you have to build the world, build the systems, build the politics, then only at the end you model how the characters interact with all of that. At which point all to often you realize that the characters probably wouldn't survive if they acted as they normally would or hadn't learned certain life lessons.<br /> <br /> This sort of shoddy modeling doesn't come across in the table top game because the players are in the moment and heavily invested due to it being their characters and their plans that they get to see interact with the world. With a tv series you might like or even love a character, but your third person perspective of the storyline unfolding makes the flaws that much more apparent. Hence why a lot of stuff feels like it falls so flat when adapted to the screen from table top games or even video games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-22T17:24:05-07:00","id":1440993,"title":"","content":"Honestly, the most likely scenario is that someone licenses the V:TM name from Paradox for a pittance, makes their own pilot and then tries to market it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-23T02:00:16-07:00","id":1441041,"title":"","content":"The worst case scenario would be what happened with World War Z, where you have an adaptation in name only that ignores the best bits of the book for a fairly generic and toothless zombie movie that (unfortunately) made just enough money for the license holders to think it might be viable for vague future sequels/spin offs, ensuring that no one else can make a faithful adaptation of any part of the original book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-23T02:23:46-07:00","id":1441046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1439995#post1439995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For my two cents, one of the major problems with adapting a game to screen be it large or small, is that what that games means changes from person to person and player to player.<br /> <br /> The long parade of Dungeons &amp; Dragons movies and TV attempts over the decades make it pretty clear that you can't hope to get close to a good product without a core storyline that everyone loves. Imagine Game of Thrones with soap opera level writing would be a high level of success, and thus far no one has even gotten close to that good.<br /> <br /> Thinking back to vampire TV series like Vampire Diaries and Forever Knight. You can't even agree on what a vampire should or should not be as far as tone or substance. Kindred the Embrace as previously mentioned was little more than 90210 with fangs. Their interpretation changed things to such a degree that ghouls and blood bonding didn't exist, Assamites only work for Prince grade or higher, vampires can day walk as long as they recently fed, the brujah were all mobsters, the gangrel acted like brujah, the nosferatu had Protean and Thaumaturgy, the list of adjustments keep going..... Needless to say there are many pitfalls to over come when it comes to any IP and V:tM has many inherent issues.<br /> <br /> Because V:tM can have any kind of tone, that means that which ever tone they pick for the show ends up excluding the fans who favor the other tones. Focus on the interpersonal drama and you get Vampire Diaries. Focus on the moral and societal decay and you get True Detective season one, focus on combat and you get the Blade tv series house of C'thon.<br /> <br /> In other words if tolkien had this sort of adaptation problem the hobbits could be interpreted as anything from their current selves to being middle earths version of Pablo Escobar opening up the middle earth markets for &quot;old toby&quot; pipe weed to dominate the party scene. Then add in a writer who wants to use the hobbits as political statement for some hippie commune for a back to the earth working the farm vibe, after which some marketing directive will come down that the plot needs to be more inclusive and that Focus Groups of people who have never read the books want to see more inclusivity and representation because that is always the take away from such groups.<br /> <br /> Perhaps I am being old and cynical, but then again if you believe the leaks regarding the development of Vampire Bloodlines 2, such issues seem to be inherent.<br /> <br /> It seems to turn into a garbage fire that is utterly divorced from the source material so reliably and so fast, you could probably set your watch to it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't know if this is a good idea but perhaps taking inspiration from the works of Lars von Trier would aid in how to portray adult subject matter in ways not done before in vampire media. Granted this would mean this show would have to get really difficult to watch with a bunch of graphic violence and sex stuff which would turn some people off.<br /> <br /> I have reservations with Netflix but the hard truth is that they have 40 million subscribers, it's unfair they have that many subs but amazon dosn't but that's the reality. This hypothetical show has to be on Netflix<br /> <br /> Also, I would go the MCU route and make this Vampire show one of 3 WoD shows set in the same city, with the other 2 being Werewolf and Mage (my favourite). Have it set in LA because Bloodline was in LA and Bloodlines is the most popular WoD media with the most popular WoD characters.<br /> <br /> for antagonists Vampire should have Hunters, Werewolf should have D.N.A or Pentex, Mage should have the Technocratic Union. when the enevitable 4th show comes and brings characters from all 3 shows together there has to be a common enemy that threatens them all. Threat Null imediatly comes to mind, but of couse WoD has a large rouges gallary. The big Thanos villan could just as easily be Antidiluvians, Earthbound, Nephandi, a pissed off Incarna, Imbued, Natural Disaster, Cthullu, or anything really.<br /> <br /> There's advantages to doing live action and there's advantages to doing animated, but I think you can get the best of both worlds if you do Rotoscoped animation ala &quot;Undone&quot; by Raphael BobWaksburg. Have it look like the Illustrations by John Van Fleet and a lot of people will leave their living rooms satisfied.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26433-ascentionthemage","name":"AscentionTheMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26433_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-23T02:34:11-07:00","id":1441047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1440025#post1440025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why license when a writer can just start from standard vampire lore and do their own thing?<br /> <br /> Other than clan names that 99% of the general population has never heard of and so will mean nothing to them and the Caine origin myth; there\u2019s nothing unique enough to VtM to make obtaining the license worth the effort.<br /> <br /> Basically, unless you want to do something with Caine and the Antediluvians (in which case your budget needs to be way bigger than most tv shows) there is zero reason not create to your own setting and focus in on just the lore elements you need to tell your particular story.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Cain TV show could work if it were animated. Get the same team that did &quot;Devilman:Crybaby&quot; and chances are you'll have a winner<br /> <br /> An alternative is that you can have a TV series based on Bloodlines in one form or another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26433-ascentionthemage","name":"AscentionTheMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26433_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-23T03:30:51-07:00","id":1441055,"title":"","content":"If White Wolf/Paradox really want to take a absurdly massive risk, they should just make the show Vampire Erotica, I don't know how sexualised Netflix would allow their shows to be but I'm confident you can Greenlit soft core porn on Netflix. Alternatively you can do hard core porn and work with Pure Taboo and make the series Premium on Pornhub. Feel free to shit on my ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26433-ascentionthemage","name":"AscentionTheMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26433_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-23T03:33:08-07:00","id":1441056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1440250#post1440250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that a V:TM protagonist should be a young hot twenty something Goth.<br /> <br /> Probably with issues against authority.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> What?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> AND WE CAN PUT IT ON THE CW!</div> </div> </div> </div>THE CW CAN GO FUCK ITSELF!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26433-ascentionthemage","name":"AscentionTheMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26433_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-23T03:40:37-07:00","id":1441057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1440363#post1440363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m going to buck the trend a bit and say if you really want to build a World of Darkness shared universe akin to the MCU... don\u2019t START with Vampire; start with Mage.<br /> <br /> Mages, particularly newly Awakened ones are, bare none, the closest to mortals in abilities and perspective to normal humans of any of the main WoD splats. That makes them ideal for an opening viewpoint character and subtle fx requirements to start.<br /> <br /> But also important is that a big part of Mage is that everything man has ever believed in exists in somewhere in the shadows. This preps the stage for the larger universe with meeting vampires, werewolves, wraiths, changelings, etc. before spinning off an associated series where we get more details on the specific supernatural type.<br /> <br /> I also really think VtM on its own just doesn\u2019t have enough unique on its own to make it a viable IP for a Netflix style series. But the larger WoD as a shared universe IS fairly unique (and rarely as well put together; ex. the Vampire Diaries and its spin-offs).</div> </div> </div> </div>This idea could also work if you have a regular Mortal, such as a SAD federal agent, or an amature vampire hunter, or a preist possilbly with the true faith ability of transubstantiation, or a recently kinfolk, or some average joe who develops Telekenisis for some reason. Damphirs and even Thinbloods could work possibly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26433-ascentionthemage","name":"AscentionTheMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26433_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-23T03:43:54-07:00","id":1441058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1440371#post1440371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously, one must start with Hunter.<br /> -Easiest to explain.<br /> -Domestic terrorism is fun for the whole family.<br /> -No factions necessary.<br /> -Main character learns as audience does.<br /> you can dive into vampire from there.<br /> -That bottom-up approach to the setting is just a good way of getting people into the zone. Just trying to explain mage politics is offputting, you just can't lead with it. Especially as, in mage, the interplay between all these different factions is important and you can't just use the Order of Hermes without... houses and technoxrats and other traditions and oh my. Vampire, at least, is largely just -the Camarilla- and you can sideline everything else till you want to use them. Hunters are perfect because you just have Robert and Jane trying to avenge their dead kids and they themselves don't even know about the SoL.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not out of the realm of possibility. Hunter has 3 videogames to its belt, which indicates a mass market appeal. Might I suggest it dosn't have to be imbued hunters, rather it could be every other Mortal hunter institutions, the CIA, the FBI, the NSA, the society of Leopold, Arcanum etc etc","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26433-ascentionthemage","name":"AscentionTheMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26433_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-23T03:50:26-07:00","id":1441059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AscentionTheMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1441055#post1441055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If White Wolf/Paradox really want to take a absurdly massive risk, they should just make the show Vampire Erotica, I don't know how sexualised Netflix would allow their shows to be but I'm confident you can Greenlit soft core porn on Netflix. Alternatively you can do hard core porn and work with Pure Taboo and make the series Premium on Pornhub. Feel free to shit on my ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure that softcore porn really is going to sell any better than anything else with the show. Mind you, it does remind me of how V:TM tried to do a erotica book and they ended up with a horror porn one with Eternal Hearts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-23T03:52:48-07:00","id":1441060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1440404#post1440404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The single biggest obstacle to a Vampire: The Masquerade tv series is probably the &quot;Elric Problem&quot;.<br /> <br /> For those that have never heard of it, Elric of Melnibone is Michael Moorcock's dark fantasy albino swordsman who has been around since the early 1960s, and one of his nicknames, &quot;The White Wolf&quot;, was the inspiration for the White Wolf Games Studios' name. There was recently an effort to get an Elric streaming series made. The problem was that everyone who looked at it said it was too much like The Witcher. The Witcher franchise, which started in the 90s, very clearly derives a lot of its influences from Elric.<br /> Vampire has a similar issue, in that ever since the first Blade movie very clearly &quot;borrowed&quot; a lot of ideas from it, too many other things look like Vampire, especially to the intellectually challenged individuals who run most entertainment studios. With Disney+ already having announced an MCU Blade streaming series (or film, I forget which), and the existence of things like the Underworld franchise, which more Hollywood type people are likely to have heard of, trying to sell them on a V:tM series would probably be an uphill battle.<br /> The likely exception is if you tried to sell them on turning LA by Night into a streaming fiction series. They might bite at that. (NPI)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;very clearly derives&quot; is putting it mildly. It's blatant Plagerism. Take it away Razorfist: <a href=\"https://youtu.be/TkiP64adGjY\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/TkiP64adGjY</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26433-ascentionthemage","name":"AscentionTheMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26433_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-23T04:05:50-07:00","id":1441062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1440528#post1440528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. I think if I were to try to make a Vampire series - let's say a Netflix style streaming one with 10 episodes - I would probably have it mainly focus on a Sire and Childe as the two main characters, with their interaction being the backbone, and their interactions with others branching off from there. Not sure which Clan, but most likely Brujah or Ventrue. <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The clan you want is Nosforatu. Nosforatu are the most Moral clan, they have to but up with a lot of bullshit because of their appearance, therefore they make for great underdogs. Nosforatus are the architects of Vampire. They're constantly developing their tunnels and their security, and, as Bertrum Tung once said, they have more going on than any clan. Whereas Ventrue are visionaries, Nosforatu are the blue collar folk that make those visions a reality. Lastly, a Nosforatu can effectivly regain their human apperance if they work hard enough at impoving their obfuscate which gives every sewer rat an ongoing arc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26433-ascentionthemage","name":"AscentionTheMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26433_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-23T09:54:53-07:00","id":1441086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AscentionTheMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1441062#post1441062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The clan you want is Nosforatu. Nosforatu are the most Moral clan, they have to but up with a lot of bullshit because of their appearance, therefore they make for great underdogs. Nosforatus are the architects of Vampire. They're constantly developing their tunnels and their security, and, as Bertrum Tung once said, they have more going on than any clan. Whereas Ventrue are visionaries, Nosforatu are the blue collar folk that make those visions a reality. Lastly, a Nosforatu can effectivly regain their human apperance if they work hard enough at impoving their obfuscate which gives every sewer rat an ongoing arc.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with nosferatu is two fold.<br /> <br /> The first is making the practical makeup viable to count as a clan weakness. In Kindred the embrace, the Nosferatu Primogen was just bald and wonky ears, there was even an episode where he put on a long haired wig while trying to court a girl and he looked normal. <br /> <br /> The second problem is of association of behaviors and traits and modern political views. The Joker movie which revolved around mental health, some how getting called an Incel indoctrination film. In the case of the Nosferatu, they spend their time creeping on everyone else, displaying classic stalker behavior, only socializing via the internet, they often resort to physical violence with Potence being a clan discipline, and lastly there is a clan tradition of using the forced embrace of a mortal like a punishment for whom ever annoys them (is it rape, mutilation, enslavement, etc.). In short the Nosferatu are three strikes in modern society, they do horrible things to others, they live in horrible places, and are horrible to look at. As long as you are a rich and good looking vampire you can always be forgiven for doing horrible things, but not the other way around it seems, or at least to the all important YA demographic.<br /> <br /> Also lets face it if the cast of Nosferatu either spend most of their time using obfuscate to look normal or their clan weakness is so poorly represented that it wouldn't considered an impediment, why exactly go through the effort of having the characters be nosferatu. You can just as easily have them be another clan with really bad havens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-23T10:00:40-07:00","id":1441087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AscentionTheMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1441055#post1441055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If White Wolf/Paradox really want to take a absurdly massive risk, they should just make the show Vampire Erotica, I don't know how sexualised Netflix would allow their shows to be but I'm confident you can Greenlit soft core porn on Netflix. Alternatively you can do hard core porn and work with Pure Taboo and make the series Premium on Pornhub. Feel free to shit on my ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>The closest you would get to that with Netflix would probably be an animated series like Castlevania or Beastars. But considering the tone deaf way Netflix handled Cuties..... yeah, I'm not holding out hope they could produce anything of value.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-23T14:28:09-07:00","id":1441131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1441041#post1441041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The worst case scenario would be what happened with World War Z, where you have an adaptation in name only that ignores the best bits of the book for a fairly generic and toothless zombie movie that (unfortunately) made just enough money for the license holders to think it might be viable for vague future sequels/spin offs, ensuring that no one else can make a faithful adaptation of any part of the original book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Max Brooks has stated that he was quite fond of the money the movie made. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-23T18:07:25-07:00","id":1441172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1441131#post1441131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Max Brooks has stated that he was quite fond of the money the movie made. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Undoubtably. But you could make several films simply from individual storylines. The helicopter pilot's story, the submarine saga, the Japanese one, and the Indian army's holding the pass in the Himalayas would all work as feature films, while several others (the Palestinian family's experiences, the family fleeing to the frozen north, the K9 units, and the feral children especially) would make excellent short films.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-23T19:32:49-07:00","id":1441182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1440368#post1440368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. Mage is probably the hardest to actually explain. It is a VERY esoteric game in terms of factions and ideas.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've been thinking about this afew days and.. I think MAGE is hard to play. But its not hard to explain on the surface level. There is a secret conspiracy of Scientists who try to kill magic. Isn't hard to grasp. The Whys of mage get into the weeds but &quot;lots of different types of magic fight back&quot; isn't deep thoughts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-23T19:51:55-07:00","id":1441184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1441182#post1441182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been thinking about this afew days and.. I think MAGE is hard to play. But its not hard to explain on the surface level. There is a secret conspiracy of Scientists who try to kill magic. Isn't hard to grasp. The Whys of mage get into the weeds but &quot;lots of different types of magic fight back&quot; isn't deep thoughts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Until you have to explain the scientists are mages too. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-23T23:47:43-07:00","id":1441200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1441086#post1441086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem with nosferatu is two fold.<br /> <br /> The first is making the practical makeup viable to count as a clan weakness. In Kindred the embrace, the Nosferatu Primogen was just bald and wonky ears, there was even an episode where he put on a long haired wig while trying to court a girl and he looked normal.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You can make the Prosphetics look more Believable by filming the show in black and white. Sci Fi film makers in the mid 20th century got away with a lot of dogshit SFX because it looked better in monochrome. I remember that asshole Moviebob talking about how Mario, Peach, and Bowser looked like they belonged in the same world because they were all represented as a collection of a few colors of pixels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26433-ascentionthemage","name":"AscentionTheMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26433_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-23T23:54:23-07:00","id":1441201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1441184#post1441184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Until you have to explain the scientists are mages too. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Technically true, but the scientists would catigorically deny this. They'd explain that what they do and what their enemies do is Enlightened Science. It might be easier to explain if this show is from the point of view of the Union.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26433-ascentionthemage","name":"AscentionTheMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26433_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-24T05:40:27-07:00","id":1441231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1441184#post1441184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Until you have to explain the scientists are mages too. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. i think you are overestimating how much a TV series really focuses on the weeds of &quot;HOW SHIT WORKS&quot; vs just giving us the broad points. Science is just a type of magic that &quot;won&quot; through murdering all who disagreed isn't super essoteric. Especially if the Union isn't the protagonist faction. They are a bunch of hypocritical murderers who want to kill all that is wonderous in the world and impose &quot;safety&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-24T09:03:23-07:00","id":1441253,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Mage is probably the least hard setting to explain at the level you\u2019d place the show\u2019s protagonists. Here\u2019s the elevator pitch explaining the Mage setting and how all the future spin-offs fit in three sentences...<br /> <br /> \u201cMagic is real and there are different ways to access it. Because of magic everything that mankind has ever believed in; vampires, werewolves, ghosts, fairies and more; exist in the shadows of the world, each with their own factions and agendas. A conspiracy of techno-mages wants to wipe out all versions of magic not accessed through science to preserve their own power in the modern world.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-24T12:29:04-07:00","id":1441285,"title":"","content":"Honestly I'd say werewolf would be the hardest to do. Heavy on Fx and wierd shit. Mage gets away with Magic is subtle more or less so you can save up for your big fights.. Werewolf each shifter needs to look good regularly. And while mage can be pretty umbra heavy it can also choose to play that down with the right protags. Wererwolf not so much. Mind you full animation might work there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-24T13:37:25-07:00","id":1441293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1441285#post1441285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Wererwolf not so much. Mind you full animation might work there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, werewolf would work much better animated, especially if you can get moody, stylistic art.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-24T14:13:33-07:00","id":1441298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1441285#post1441285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I'd say werewolf would be the hardest to do. Heavy on Fx and wierd shit. Mage gets away with Magic is subtle more or less so you can save up for your big fights.. Werewolf each shifter needs to look good regularly. And while mage can be pretty umbra heavy it can also choose to play that down with the right protags. Wererwolf not so much. Mind you full animation might work there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Teen Wolf was done in 2011 and is a pretty decent horror werewolf show.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-