et=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-25T07:27:26-07:00","id":1441371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1441349#post1441349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, I don't think the werewolf fights should be the most important element. Less CGI and more character development.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So.. no dueling. No Ranking up. No combatting the wyrm wherever it breeds and dwells. Even if you spend most of the time on other things Fighting in some fashion is pretty much the central element Everything else falls out from there. A whole season might fall out of an Alpha challenge... but that still means doing something with that.<br /> <br /> And even ignoring fighting the Umbra is much more.. there. You probably couldn't do that live action practically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-25T08:43:59-07:00","id":1441376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1441371#post1441371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So.. no dueling. No Ranking up. No combatting the wyrm wherever it breeds and dwells. Even if you spend most of the time on other things Fighting in some fashion is pretty much the central element Everything else falls out from there. A whole season might fall out of an Alpha challenge... but that still means doing something with that.<br /> <br /> And even ignoring fighting the Umbra is much more.. there. You probably couldn't do that live action practically.</div> </div> </div> </div>That kind of nails the issue of how everyone's game is something different. My werewolf is more about Garou politics, tradition vs. reform, kinfolk, and corporate warfare. The big problem with adapting RPGs is they're toolsets as much as settings.<br /> <br /> I think HEART OF THE FOREST is the greatest werewolf property ever and I played it with only one act of violence and one change over 4 hours.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-25T13:30:56-07:00","id":1441414,"title":"","content":"The issue is that Garou politics, in a vacuum, are just going to seem silly if you don't show the umbra and the murderfest. The big thing with Garou is, well, RAGE, and how the fuck do you show RAGE if you aren't murdering the fuck out of some suspected formor every odd tuesday? How do you show the spiritual side, the umbra, or shapeshifting, on a budget? Most of the socially interesting things about the Garou only work in context of them being absolute murder-machines who make deals with spirits, the rest of it is just them being a cult/alliance of cults with questionable treatment of second class citizens. Nobody who hasn't read a corebook is going to zone in on the finer points of garou politics, like the differences between Get and Fianna, how silver fangs plan to deal with their inbreeding problem, and the fact that the wendigo exist, if they're not at least sucked in by all the stuff that distinguishes Werewolf from Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-25T15:35:07-07:00","id":1441423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1441376#post1441376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That kind of nails the issue of how everyone's game is something different. My werewolf is more about Garou politics, tradition vs. reform, kinfolk, and corporate warfare. The big problem with adapting RPGs is they're toolsets as much as settings.<br /> <br /> I think HEART OF THE FOREST is the greatest werewolf property ever and I played it with only one act of violence and one change over 4 hours.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If you can get across &quot;at anytime Garou might freak out and rip off the limbs of someone they care&quot; without showing transformation you are a better man than me. You are an audience built knowing the setting Knowing the stakes so they don't have to show it to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-26T00:36:56-07:00","id":1441469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1441285#post1441285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I'd say werewolf would be the hardest to do. Heavy on Fx and wierd shit. Mage gets away with Magic is subtle more or less so you can save up for your big fights.. Werewolf each shifter needs to look good regularly. And while mage can be pretty umbra heavy it can also choose to play that down with the right protags. Wererwolf not so much. Mind you full animation might work there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wrote ua forum post talking about exactly what you're talking about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26433-ascentionthemage","name":"AscentionTheMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26433_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-26T00:39:23-07:00","id":1441470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1441299#post1441299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, but werewolf isn't just the odd transformation, it's the umbra and banes and a whole world that would really just look better with gritty animation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but the Werewolves in teen wolf look like very hairy humans with sharp teeth, wheras Garou look like they regularly get into fistfights with the Incredible Hulk or Juggernaught.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26433-ascentionthemage","name":"AscentionTheMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26433_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-26T00:41:46-07:00","id":1441471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1441346#post1441346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Every major and quite a large number of minor cast members need to have at least Crinos, Hispo fully done in cgi with maybe galabro done practically and... trainned wolves? That is before the wierdness of the umbra. Mage could get away with having an umbra episode being rare I can't say the same would be for werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are wolves that are comfortable around humans, but I don't know if they can be trained. I know in Game of Thrones they used a breed of dog that looks like a wolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26433-ascentionthemage","name":"AscentionTheMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26433_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-26T00:43:23-07:00","id":1441472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1441371#post1441371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So.. no dueling. No Ranking up. No combatting the wyrm wherever it breeds and dwells. Even if you spend most of the time on other things Fighting in some fashion is pretty much the central element Everything else falls out from there. A whole season might fall out of an Alpha challenge... but that still means doing something with that.<br /> <br /> And even ignoring fighting the Umbra is much more.. there. You probably couldn't do that live action practically.</div> </div> </div> </div>At that point you might as well cut out werewolves entierly and focus exclusivly on a kinfolk fellowship straight out of the Kinfolk sourcebook","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26433-ascentionthemage","name":"AscentionTheMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26433_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-26T00:44:36-07:00","id":1441473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1441376#post1441376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That kind of nails the issue of how everyone's game is something different. My werewolf is more about Garou politics, tradition vs. reform, kinfolk, and corporate warfare. The big problem with adapting RPGs is they're toolsets as much as settings.<br /> <br /> I think HEART OF THE FOREST is the greatest werewolf property ever and I played it with only one act of violence and one change over 4 hours.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heart of the forest &gt; earthblood","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26433-ascentionthemage","name":"AscentionTheMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26433_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-26T08:35:54-07:00","id":1441509,"title":"","content":"All of the above is definitely why Mage would be the most practical thing to adapt first. Everyone is human and, generally, a part of contemporary culture so no special wardrobes or prosthetics would be needed.<br /> <br /> As an added bonus, \u201cranking up\u201d in skill for a new Mage means going from probably fairly vulgar effects on first awakening (so flashy fx for the first episode to draw viewers in) to learning to use coincidental effects (i.e. minor or even no fx needed).<br /> <br /> In other words, cutting your fx costs for later episodes can be portrayed as the protagonists getting BETTER at magic. That\u2019s a huge advantage in terms of being able to sell a series to the bean counters.<br /> <br /> People mock the idea of a CW series, but it\u2019s worth considering how the Arrowverse got itself off the ground. \u201cArrow\u201d was grounded, down to earth and, most importantly, far less expensive in terms of production relative to \u201cSmallville\u201d which also derived from the same DC source precisely because it was a hero where they could rely on mostly practical effects and stunts (no super strength or speed or heat vision or freeze breath or x-ray vision to portray). As such, it was a fairly safe bet in terms of getting the series greenlit because it\u2019s production costs would be pretty typical of any other action oriented series.<br /> <br /> Only once it was established as a hit did they expand out to The Flash with its bigger FX budget (and one main super power), then once that was established it was Legends of Tomorrow (a whole team of supers) and Supergirl (a team\u2019s worth of powers in one character... also launched on CBS with a much bigger budget than a CW series), by the time we got Stargirl and Superman &amp; Lois both series were being primarily produced not for the CW but as streaming content for HBOmax with comparatively higher budgets and production values.<br /> <br /> The point of which is, if you want to grow the World of Darkness into its own franchise, you need to start not necessarily with the biggest name in the stable, but with the one it\u2019s easiest to get investors to back as a reasonable risk, but which also has enough from similar faire so it can be seen as a launching point for a larger universe.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s partly why I think Mage is a stronger starting option than anything hunter-related. Arrow got itself noticed by doing a grounded and realistic take on a vigilante superhero; a novel take coming off Smallville and with the lighter tones of the early MCU at the time). I just don\u2019t think there\u2019s enough with mortal hunters to set it apart from the likes of say, Supernatural, in its budget range.<br /> <br /> By contrast, I think something akin to The Fugitive with Magic could be something that would stand out. Have the protagonists hunted by mysterious government agents (black suits, black cars, black helicopters) while meeting various covert magic factions (i.e. the Traditions) as they learn to use their magic subtly and stay off the radar as they help people while staying one step ahead of the MIBs (the only face of those hunting them at first) and eventually learning the true nature of what hunts them... i.e. that they\u2019re really a cabal of techno-mages bent on eliminating the competition.<br /> <br /> Along the way you introduce vampires and werewolves and ghosts and fairies and hunters and demons and mummies, etc. with an eye to spinning those out into other series once the foundation is proven.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-26T09:17:24-07:00","id":1441511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/mai