to The Fugitive with Magic could be something that would stand out. Have the protagonists hunted by mysterious government agents (black suits, black cars, black helicopters) while meeting various covert magic factions (i.e. the Traditions) as they learn to use their magic subtly and stay off the radar as they help people while staying one step ahead of the MIBs (the only face of those hunting them at first) and eventually learning the true nature of what hunts them... i.e. that they\u2019re really a cabal of techno-mages bent on eliminating the competition.<br /> <br /> Along the way you introduce vampires and werewolves and ghosts and fairies and hunters and demons and mummies, etc. with an eye to spinning those out into other series once the foundation is proven.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree but Arrow is the worst show of all time. The CW network makes a lot of garbage aimed at Melodrama hungry simps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26433-ascentionthemage","name":"AscentionTheMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26433_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-26T10:53:27-07:00","id":1441528,"title":"","content":"Wraith works too as they they think and act like mortals. Regular ass mortals would be tge most relatable, but you can't do that unless you do &quot;Human: the protaganist&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26433-ascentionthemage","name":"AscentionTheMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26433_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-26T12:26:21-07:00","id":1441539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1441511#post1441511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think vampire is much more likely to be adaptable because vampires are cool without special effects while mages aren't.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, blood and wounds there from are special effects.<br /> <br /> Also, parasites taking advantage of and feeding on hapless mortals is NOT cool or a good look in the present days.<br /> <br /> You don\u2019t want protagonists with an end goal of \u201cbecome a blood instead of sex version of Weinstein, Epstein or [insert crony capitalist/government dirt bag here] only get away with it\u201d as the end goal for your protagonist these days.<br /> <br /> Even the CW couldn\u2019t sell that these days... which is why The Originals (where the vampires were pretty much monsters with protagonist-centered morality to justify it) gave way to Legacies where the protagonists protect ordinary humans from monsters and vampires even feeding from humans is portrayed as morally degenerate.<br /> <br /> In the 90\u2019s after the Soviet Union collapsed, America kicked Iraq\u2019s ass, the giant sucking sound of corporate greed hadn\u2019t started hollowing out what\u2019s now the Rust Belt, and the message that endless peacekeeping wars were a good thing was still fresh enough to be plausible; Gen-Xers had the luxury of sympathizing with vampires forced to feed from the innocent to survive.<br /> <br /> These days people don\u2019t sympathize with the crony capitalists, the short-selling vulture investors who steal people\u2019s jobs just to pad portfolios already stuffed with more than they can spend in a lifetime, with elites who victimize women and children for their twisted pleasures. The government and law enforcement who abuse their power and target helpless citizens because they believe they won\u2019t be held accountable. They don\u2019t care about how angsty they might be over their heinous acts.<br /> <br /> No, they want those assholes burned to the ground and vampires are charactures of every last one of the dirtbags people are pretty much done with (to paraphrase a discussion about Legacies vs. Vampire Dairies that demonstrates the spirit of the age; if Damon started one of his pity murder sprees that was a staple of TVD to show how tormented and miserable he was on Legacies, the audience wouldn\u2019t be expected to sympathize, they\u2019d be cheering after Hope beheaded him before the fourth message break of the episode).<br /> <br /> VtM as written is toxic in the current entertainment environment. If your vampires aren\u2019t of the friendly neighborhood variety right now they\u2019re only going to be usable as villains for actual protagonists to slay. Seriously, try finding something featuring vampires in the last decade or so that hasn\u2019t either portrayed them as monsters to be destroyed (ex. 28 Days of Night, Van Helsing) or softened them down to friendly neighborhood levels (ex. Vampire Academy, Legacies, Twilight). Even the proposed Disney+ Blade series is about a vampire HUNTER with vampires as villains.<br /> <br /> Short version; vampires aren\u2019t cool protagonists these days outside of the skewed demographics of a forum about a game where you play vampires (where comments are mostly limited to the same half-dozen or so people again and again).<br /> <br /> If you want a WoD shared universe to get off the ground in the present day you\u2019re going to need GENUINE protagonists to launch with, not villain protagonists like VtMs vampires. Hunters (of the HH variety) and Mages are the lowest production budget options for those with some wraiths and werewolves as runners up if you had a bigger budget.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-26T12:47:31-07:00","id":1441542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1441539#post1441539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, blood and wounds there from are special effects.<br /> <br /> Also, parasites taking advantage of and feeding on hapless mortals is NOT cool or a good look in the present days.<br /> <br /> You don\u2019t want protagonists with an end goal of \u201cbecome a blood instead of sex version of Weinstein, Epstein or [insert crony capitalist/government dirt bag here] only get away with it\u201d as the end goal for your protagonist these days.<br /> <br /> Even the CW couldn\u2019t sell that these days... which is why The Originals (where the vampires were pretty much monsters with protagonist-centered morality to justify it) gave way to Legacies where the protagonists protect ordinary humans from monsters and vampires even feeding from humans is portrayed as morally degenerate.<br /> <br /> In the 90\u2019s after the Soviet Union collapsed, America kicked Iraq\u2019s ass, the giant sucking sound of corporate greed hadn\u2019t started hollowing out what\u2019s now the Rust Belt, and the message that endless peacekeeping wars were a good thing was still fresh enough to be plausible; Gen-Xers had the luxury of sympathizing with vampires forced to feed from the innocent to survive.<br /> <br /> These days people don\u2019t sympathize with the crony capitalists, the short-selling vulture investors who steal people\u2019s jobs just to pad portfolios already stuffed with more than they can spend in a lifetime, with elites who victimize women and children for their twisted pleasures. The government and law enforcement who abuse their power and target helpless citizens because they believe they won\u2019t be held accountable. They don\u2019t care about how angsty they might be over their heinous acts.<br /> <br /> No, they want those assholes burned to the ground and vampires are charactures of every last one of the dirtbags people are pretty much done with (to paraphrase a discussion about Legacies vs. Vampire Dairies that demonstrates the spirit of the age; if Damon started one of his pity murder sprees that was a staple of TVD to show how tormented and miserable he was on Legacies, the audience wouldn\u2019t be expected to sympathize, they\u2019d be cheering after Hope beheaded him before the fourth message break of the episode).<br /> <br /> VtM as written is toxic in the current entertainment environment. If your vampires aren\u2019t of the friendly neighborhood variety right now they\u2019re only going to be usable as villains for actual protagonists to slay. Seriously, try finding something featuring vampires in the last decade or so that hasn\u2019t either portrayed them as monsters to be destroyed (ex. 28 Days of Night, Van Helsing) or softened them down to friendly neighborhood levels (ex. Vampire Academy, Legacies, Twilight). Even the proposed Disney+ Blade series is about a vampire HUNTER with vampires as villains.<br /> <br /> Short version; vampires aren\u2019t cool protagonists these days outside of the skewed demographics of a forum about a game where you play vampires (where comments are mostly limited to the same half-dozen or so people again and again).<br /> <br /> If you want a WoD shared universe to get off the ground in the present day you\u2019re going to need GENUINE protagonists to launch with, not villain protagonists like VtMs vampires. Hunters (of the HH variety) and Mages are the lowest production budget options for those with some wraiths and werewolves as runners up if you had a bigger budget.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with your analysis. Although I find Vampire lore fascinating, I much prefer actually playing changelings or mages, and both of my vampires (Charity, a Tremere, and Julia, an Ancient Roman Ventrue) were sort of friendly neighborhood Twilight vampires who never fed from unwilling mortals (Charity had a small Herd who willingly let her drink their blood in exchange for hanging out with them and being cool and teaching them some magic, and for most of the campaign Julia had a relationship with her handmaid and close friend Marcia where Julia fed from Marcia and in return gave her Vitae to turn her into a ghoul which I\u2019m not sure is legit under V20 rules but we did it anyway).<br /> <br /> Sorry. That was a rant but basically I agree with you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25665,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 03-26-2021, 03:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-26T13:40:03-07:00","id":1441550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1441539#post1441539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want a WoD shared universe to get off the ground in the present day you\u2019re going to need GENUINE protagonists to launch with, not villain protagonists like VtMs vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since when have TV shows had to be about good protagonists? HBO made a show about guys in the Mafia and people love it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-26T16:32:10-07:00","id":1441569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1441550#post1441550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since when have TV shows had to be about good protagonists? HBO made a show about guys in the Mafia and people love it.</div> </div> </div> </div>George W. Bush was still President and the Wall Street collapse was still in the future when The Sopranos went off the air; 14 years ago.<br /> <br /> Tastes in entertainment change with the times. Generally, people enjoy darker faire during good times (when it\u2019s safe) and more hopeful faire when times are bad. We are not in good times these days and so tastes in entertainment have shifted to match.<br /> <br /> Look at what people are excited about in genre television these days; the Mandalorian (particularly Luke freaking Skywalker showing up), Snyder\u2019s Justice League, Superman &amp; Lois, Falcon &amp; Winter Soldier, etc.<br /> <br /> These are just not the times where villain protagonists, particularly those victimizing the poor and disadvantaged from positions of ill-gotten wealth and power, are going to draw in the numbers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-27T07:54:24-07:00","id":1441640,"title":"","content":"Vampire can be extremely low budget in regards to special effects. <br /> There's that &quot;:<i>The Masquerade</i>&quot; part, after all.<br /> <br /> <br /> Only Potence and Protean actually requires money to pull off, but you aren't going to show them off as often as, say, Dominate. Animalism has one power that actually needs money, the rest is just Dominate with more interesting acting. Vicissitude, yes, I love it, but it's not really something most Camarilla come in contact with and you can safely put it off till your show is successful and people aren't afraid of pumping money into it. Obtenebration can be easy (It's black, it's all black) and Chimestry is, well, you just use props normally. <br /> <br /> But yes, The Masquerade. The whole deal is they be low-key and subtle about them being vampires. That means not showing off your powers, that means on some scenes, the actors try not to breath except to take in air, that means someone launches a Dominate and there are no special effects telling viewers who just got Dominated. It also means you don't have to spend lots of money on period costumes and goth paraphernalia. The prince can wear a business casual and doesn't need to put on a silly prince voice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-27T08:23:00-07:00","id":1441641,"title":"","content":"Or we could just eschew a filmed live series anyway, and go animated for whatever. Castlevania and Blood of Zeus did great on Netflix, and they fund anime and other animation-driven shows a lot. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-27T09:09:16-07:00","id":1441653,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> do you have anything you want to add? Or have you already said everything you need to on this subject?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-27T12:25:07-07:00","id":1441673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1441653#post1441653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> do you have anything you want to add? Or have you already said everything you need to on this subject?</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally, my perspective on the subject is influenced by my opinion as a genre writer and the fact that I actually almost had my Supervillainy Saga books picked up by Michael Bay's company (we had a few phone calls so, &quot;almost picked up&quot; is perhaps stretching it). My books being a parody of the MCU and superheroes in general so representing the sort of &quot;lower tier&quot; intellectual property that can get bought up and potentially made much bigger.<br /> <br /> For me, people are absolutely correct that Vampire: The Masquerade is not something that is 100% necessary for anyone going to make a vampire show as plenty of modern vampires are influenced by it (and its derivatives) already. It also started as a toolkit to be able to gather all forms of vampire media together as well. So much so when Underworld WAS sued over it, the reaction even from fellow geeks was not complimentary.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://photos.smugmug.com/photos/215473652_PbFNx-L-2.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Hell, my own writing in urban fantasy owes itself to White Wolf giving me a bunch of ideas and I drew from the Sookie Stackhouse Mysteries, Laurel K. Hamilton, and other worlds similar to White Wolf. That isn't actually a BAD thing for any future adaptations, though. Because the thing about this is creating a market for the genre is a good thing.<br /> <br /> Forever Knight<br /> Teen Wolf<br /> Moonlight<br /> Buffy the Vampire Slayer/Angel<br /> The Vampire Diaries/The Originals<br /> Supernatural (which was going to have a White Wolf-based &quot;warring Lupines and Werewolves in Chicago&quot; spin off, I shit you not)<br /> <br /> All of these things are pretty similar to what a White Wolf show would be like but they don't make it HARDER to do a spin off, quite the contrary, they give any potential makers of a WOD show an in to pitch the show. I'm pretty sure that the process will consist of White Wolf assembling their own pitch and licensing it to a smaller company that is looking to break big but that's not a bad thing. I also suspect that it will probably be more likely to be done by fans of the video game than the other.<br /> <br /> But I think the odds are quite good, IMHO, that they're laying the groundwork for it now. Still, I wouldn't be surprised if the V:TM show is created first in Europe and then adapted in America later.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> <b>Some Additional Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> I'm actually of the mind we already HAVE the V:TM TV show in <b>LA By Night</b>. It's an unconventional show consisting of freeform roleplaying but the first episode on Youtube (which is after its successful run on Twitch) has a million views. It's also a four hour long show and that's pretty fucking impressive.<br /> It's also an adaptation of a tabletop game anyway so watching people roleplaying Geek and Sundry style doesn't mean it's NOT a TV show that's adapted from a video game. It certainly benefited the brand and is probably responsible for 50% of the positive name recognition of V5 after a rocky start.<br /> <br /> I personally would also always adapt V:TM first because of not only the name recognition but simply because I do think of it as the &quot;best&quot; game. Still, I think it'll be creator driven so if someone wanted to do Wraith: The Oblivion the TV show first because the guy likes that game more than he'll do Wraith: The Oblivion more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-27-2021, 03:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-27T12:31:31-07:00","id":1441675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1441569#post1441569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are just not the times where villain protagonists, particularly those victimizing the poor and disadvantaged from positions of ill-gotten wealth and power, are going to draw in the numbers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then do a game about Anarchs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps