Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-27T13:46:55-07:00","id":1441689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1441539#post1441539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, blood and wounds there from are special effects.<br /> <br /> Also, parasites taking advantage of and feeding on hapless mortals is NOT cool or a good look in the present days.<br /> <br /> You don\u2019t want protagonists with an end goal of \u201cbecome a blood instead of sex version of Weinstein, Epstein or [insert crony capitalist/government dirt bag here] only get away with it\u201d as the end goal for your protagonist these days.<br /> <br /> Even the CW couldn\u2019t sell that these days... which is why The Originals (where the vampires were pretty much monsters with protagonist-centered morality to justify it) gave way to Legacies where the protagonists protect ordinary humans from monsters and vampires even feeding from humans is portrayed as morally degenerate.<br /> <br /> In the 90\u2019s after the Soviet Union collapsed, America kicked Iraq\u2019s ass, the giant sucking sound of corporate greed hadn\u2019t started hollowing out what\u2019s now the Rust Belt, and the message that endless peacekeeping wars were a good thing was still fresh enough to be plausible; Gen-Xers had the luxury of sympathizing with vampires forced to feed from the innocent to survive.<br /> <br /> These days people don\u2019t sympathize with the crony capitalists, the short-selling vulture investors who steal people\u2019s jobs just to pad portfolios already stuffed with more than they can spend in a lifetime, with elites who victimize women and children for their twisted pleasures. The government and law enforcement who abuse their power and target helpless citizens because they believe they won\u2019t be held accountable. They don\u2019t care about how angsty they might be over their heinous acts.<br /> <br /> No, they want those assholes burned to the ground and vampires are charactures of every last one of the dirtbags people are pretty much done with (to paraphrase a discussion about Legacies vs. Vampire Dairies that demonstrates the spirit of the age; if Damon started one of his pity murder sprees that was a staple of TVD to show how tormented and miserable he was on Legacies, the audience wouldn\u2019t be expected to sympathize, they\u2019d be cheering after Hope beheaded him before the fourth message break of the episode).<br /> <br /> VtM as written is toxic in the current entertainment environment. If your vampires aren\u2019t of the friendly neighborhood variety right now they\u2019re only going to be usable as villains for actual protagonists to slay. Seriously, try finding something featuring vampires in the last decade or so that hasn\u2019t either portrayed them as monsters to be destroyed (ex. 28 Days of Night, Van Helsing) or softened them down to friendly neighborhood levels (ex. Vampire Academy, Legacies, Twilight). Even the proposed Disney+ Blade series is about a vampire HUNTER with vampires as villains.<br /> <br /> Short version; vampires aren\u2019t cool protagonists these days outside of the skewed demographics of a forum about a game where you play vampires (where comments are mostly limited to the same half-dozen or so people again and again).<br /> <br /> If you want a WoD shared universe to get off the ground in the present day you\u2019re going to need GENUINE protagonists to launch with, not villain protagonists like VtMs vampires. Hunters (of the HH variety) and Mages are the lowest production budget options for those with some wraiths and werewolves as runners up if you had a bigger budget.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are ways to get around vampires being predators of the innocent. One path being you can make your protags concentualists, feeding from blood donated to them from volunteers. Another is the Spike route, only feed from animals blood. A third is for your protags to be villans for villans, feeding off scumbags or even other vampires. The last method is to rely on someone who has the supernatural ability to produce cruelty free blood, any catholic preist with enough true faith can preform Transubstantiation for Vampires who agree to walk a more virtuous path.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26433-ascentionthemage","user":"AscentionTheMage","date":".  Fixin typos. 03-27-2021, 04:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26433-ascentionthemage","name":"AscentionTheMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26433_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"da