r\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AscentionTheMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1441698#post1441698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not a fan of extreme body horror are we?<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>-plays Tzmisce-<br /> &quot;You know I'm something of an extremist myself&quot;<br /> <br /> (I didn't like it for other reasons)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-27T15:31:10-07:00","id":1441713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1441708#post1441708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-plays Tzmisce-<br /> &amp;quot;You know I'm something of an extremist myself&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> (I didn't like it for other reasons)</div> </div> </div> </div>I dislike that you dislike the show, but I will tolerate it because everyone has diffrent tastes and sensibilities. I will say however you're missing out on a killer ending.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26433-ascentionthemage","name":"AscentionTheMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26433_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-27T15:57:01-07:00","id":1441716,"title":"","content":"So I'd run a series with interconnected groups. First season we get the neonate going through the basics learning from the bullshit and being oppressed we see the build up as there are a lot of younger vampires and all the power is in the hands of the Elders who can and do execute them when there's &quot;too many&quot;. We see a parallel story of the Elders basically keeping cap on things they aren't &quot;Opressors&quot; they are hard people making hard choices...<br /> <br /> Then we see the third story. The Second Inquisition slowly pealing back the masquerade as the two sides butt heads. Whole season leads to a clusterfuck three way fight completely obliterating the hunters but also seriously cutting down the cast of vampires to have them being extremely careful about politicing because while we know they crushed the local SI they don't. They don't know what is going on. <br /> <br /> So you have new oportunities for many of the neonates as the city shakes out the new status quo moving into the big scale vampire politicing now with openings for view point character.<br /> <br /> And then have an after credit scene some where of one of the SI guys who died waking up in a tube.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-27T15:57:03-07:00","id":1441717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AscentionTheMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1441689#post1441689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are ways to get around vampires being predators of the innocent. One path being you can make your protags concentualists, feeding from blood donated to them from volunteers. Another is the Spike route, only feed from animals blood. A third is for your protags to be villans for villans, feeding off scumbags or even other vampires. The last method is to rely on someone who has the supernatural ability to produce cruelty free blood, any catholic preist with enough true faith can preform Transubstantiation for Vampires who agree to walk a more virtuous path.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I call complete bullshit on the whole, &quot;Antiheroes aren't popular&quot; thing. Game of Thrones' most popular characters were Cersei and Jaime. There's Succession on HBO right now.<br /> <br /> People LOVE antiheroes and villain protagonists.<br /> <br /> There was a massive Netflix success about a woman exploiting old people for their possessions starring Rosamund Pike and a half-dozen other thrillers right now about privileged assholes. I just got done watching THE ONE which is about a fraudulent tech billionaire getting away with murder.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AscentionTheMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1441694#post1441694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Meh. Though the show was just Detroit: Become Human. [</div> </div> </div> </div>Bizarre factoid: Detroit Beyond Human was partially inspired by HUMANS.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1441695#post1441695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">WoD works best as Our world, made worse by literal monsters, than it does as a DnD romp. An exaggerated truth rather than pure fantasy, if you will. </span></span></span><br /> While in general historical accuracy has improved over the years with people enthused by insightful youtube historians, it's not good enough. Vikings is, for some reason, remains very popular, and DAV20 was very liberal with it's history (disrespectful I'd say, but nobody wants to stand up for small european nations filled with white people, lest they be confused with something/the book had a small audience)<br /> <br /> In other words, don't touch the dark ages (outside maybe small flashbacks for a modern series)</div> </div> </div> </div>Because people don't give a shit about historical accuracy. It's why I hate the pretenious Ubisoft has to it. There's nothing remotely historical about their interpretation of Vikings or Ancient Greece.<br /> <br /> I don't mind fake history but don't pretend it's remotely true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-27-2021, 07:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-28T04:17:33-07:00","id":1441769,"title":"","content":"Ubisoft were pretty good about it for their first few AC games. Mind you the Assassin/Templar plot was the height of pretentious and passe material, nevermind the ancient aliens. Still, renaissance Italy looked spectacular and you could really appreciate the detail gone into it.<br /> <br /> Actual-history looks good, even if you're not an aficionado it has an intangible quality to it that works well. And, well, it's not first edition anymore where vampires are responsible for everything in the mortal world (well, uh... let's ignore V5 and it's insistence on being current and stick to the editions that were actually tactful) The vampires became less instigators of history and more respondents and opportunists.<br /> <br /> Anyway, with your attitude; don't touch the dark ages. simple as that. A few people care for history, a few people also care that their homeland isn't made into a crude charicature or totally whitewashed. Nobody wants to see their people represented as fur covered savages or worse, modern Americans, for the sake of a US based audience who couldn't give a genuine shit about other cultures.<br /> <br /> (Also historical dramas are very often legit-good.)<br /> At the very least let me pine over good costumes. Everyone loves good costumes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-28T07:16:01-07:00","id":1441771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1441769#post1441769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ubisoft were pretty good about it for their first few AC games. Mind you the Assassin/Templar plot was the height of pretentious and passe material, nevermind the ancient aliens. Still, renaissance Italy looked spectacular and you could really appreciate the detail gone into it.<br /> <br /> Actual-history looks good, even if you're not an aficionado it has an intangible quality to it that works well. And, well, it's not first edition anymore where vampires are responsible for everything in the mortal world (well, uh... let's ignore V5 and it's insistence on being current and stick to the editions that were actually tactful) The vampires became less instigators of history and more respondents and opportunists.<br /> <br /> Anyway, with your attitude; don't touch the dark ages. simple as that. A few people care for history, a few people also care that their homeland isn't made into a crude charicature or totally whitewashed. Nobody wants to see their people represented as fur covered savages or worse, modern Americans, for the sake of a US based audience who couldn't give a genuine shit about other cultures.<br /> <br /> (Also historical dramas are very often legit-good.)<br /> At the very least let me pine over good costumes. Everyone loves good costumes.</div> </div> </div> </div>FYI - I am a Master of History.<br /> <br /> I do not turn to a game about vampires for my history. I don't want historical accuracy because a world with vampires, mages, and changelings would not be historically accurate. And find it weird people would pretend otherwise.<br /> <br /> Any Dark Ages should be full of magic, uindead, eldritch locations, hidden cults of surviving pagans, spectral battlefields, and off the wall craziness.<br /> <br /> But YMMV, obviously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-28-2021, 10:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-28T07:21:08-07:00","id":1441772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1441769#post1441769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A few people care for history, a few people also care that their homeland isn't made into a crude charicature or totally whitewashed. Nobody wants to see their people represented as fur covered savages</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be interested to see what you're talking about. Is this in DAV20? Not that I think Dark Ages Vampire show would initially viable. Sell conspirational vampires or medieval fantasy, but who wants both combined if they aren't already into one of them?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-28T07:30:19-07:00","id":1441774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1440084#post1440084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then we think back to the Highlander tv series where we had only one type of immortal, the same set of rules for all, and only a few instances of magical items or extra powers. If people can't connect to that much of a simplified immortal story, yeah WoD is more or less unusable.<br /> <br /> Also the Supernatural tv series more or less cornered the Hunter storyline spot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which leaves a lot of fans for people who want more of the same now that ot's over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-28T08:47:20-07:00","id":1441776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1441769#post1441769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ubisoft were pretty good about it for their first few AC games. Mind you the Assassin/Templar plot was the height of pretentious and passe material, nevermind the ancient aliens. Still, renaissance Italy looked spectacular and you could really appreciate the detail gone into it.<br /> <br /> Actual-history looks good, even if you're not an aficionado it has an intangible quality to it that works well. And, well, it's not first edition anymore where vampires are responsible for everything in the mortal world (well, uh... let's ignore V5 and it's insistence on being current and stick to the editions that were actually tactful) The vampires became less instigators of history and more respondents and opportunists.<br /> <br /> Anyway, with your attitude; don't touch the dark ages. simple as that. A few people care for history, a few people also care that their homeland isn't made into a crude charicature or totally whitewashed. Nobody wants to see their people represented as fur covered savages or worse, modern Americans, for the sake of a US based audience who couldn't give a genuine shit about other cultures.<br /> <br /> (Also historical dramas are very often legit-good.)<br /> At the very least let me pine over good costumes. Everyone loves good costumes.</div> </div> </div> </div>The series would be better off if it were a trillogy focusing on the conflict between sarasins and templars, excluding the modern age and animus bullshit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26433-ascentionthemage","name":"AscentionTheMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26433_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-28T10:48:59-07:00","id":1441781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AscentionTheMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1441776#post1441776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The series would be better off if it were a trillogy focusing on the conflict between sarasins and templars, excluding the modern age and animus bullshit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the Crusades AC was the worst of the series, though. Besides, neither order has any similarity to their historical counterparts.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-28T12:18:57-07:00","id":1441794,"title":"","content":"The crusades AC was the worst of the series (That i've played at least, haven't touched anything past the american one) because they were first and thus more of a tech demo than an actual game. Not for any problem with the setting. (The later games have some serious setting problems... yeesh) <br /> <br /> I'm not saying everything needs to be a perfectly historical setting, but I'd really like to move on from nobody bathes, everyone wears brown, warriors wear leather, christians are evil and non-christians are liberals / women can't breath in corsets, people throw their shit out the window, and the british are stupid for fighting in line formation/anything in a mel gibson movie.<br /> <br /> But... yeah... better just... not touch DAV. DAV is a spin-off, not the main series. It works for flashbacks, so you can do that -Remember the time we raided Chorazin/fought in the omen wa/survived the inquisition- rather than follow mithras and his multi-millenia reign. <br /> <br /> <br /> Launching the series mid-V5 would be a terrible idea too. <br /> -You actually want to start it a bit further back so you can zoom through the downtime and the torpors; starting 2021 gives you no room. <br /> -Most of the V5 metaplot changes work with the normal setting as context. You can start with the Tremere blown up for a game, but it's kinda shitty to do that for a TV show. What does it mean for the Tremere to be blown up? (also, like, yeah, V5 jumped the shark hard by putting all theses high-potential metaplot twists in the past between editions where they're all done and dusted; I wanna kill augustus as necromancer, not rise from torpor to find he's dead; that just feels like i've been robbed of vengance)<br /> -SAD and the SoL are just way cooler as individual organizations than the 2nd Inq, and it'd be easier to introduce them to audiences individually rather than as a web/blob.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-28T12:35:34-07:00","id":1441795,"title":"","content":"Honestly a Dark ages Vampire played as &quot;Game of thrones.. but with vampires&quot; seems like it might feed a niche that isn't getting fed. There are plenty of semihistorical series and at least a Vampire can justify living through ALL THE COOL PARTS of the viking age. Plus its a pretty easy elevator Pitch: &quot;Game of thrones.. with Vampires&quot; and you can better justify it not being historically accurate.. because there's vampires running around covering up the real history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-28T12:35:53-07:00","id":1441797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1441794#post1441794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Launching the series mid-V5 would be a terrible idea too.<br /> -You actually want to start it a bit further back so you can zoom through the downtime and the torpors; starting 2021 gives you no room.<br /> -Most of the V5 metaplot changes work with the normal setting as context. You can start with the Tremere blown up for a game, but it's kinda shitty to do that for a TV show. What does it mean for the Tremere to be blown up? (also, like, yeah, V5 jumped the shark hard by putting all theses high-potential metaplot twists in the past between editions where they're all done and dusted; I wanna kill augustus as necromancer, not rise from torpor to find he's dead; that just feels like i've been robbed of vengance)<br /> -SAD and the SoL are just way cooler as individual organizations than the 2nd Inq, and it'd be easier to introduce them to audiences individually rather than as a web/blob.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I think the visual novels and LA By Night show that the simplifications of V5 for televison and mass media are very easily incorporated:<br /> <br /> * Vampires have a Masquerade because humans are hunting them and have assault rifles<br /> * Anarchs oppose the Camarilla<br /> * The Tremere are a bunch of feuding wizard houses.<br /> * Neonate vampires are important enough to effect things<br /> <br /> Really, it seems V5 was made to make the gameworld very easy to understand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-28T19:11:39-07:00","id":1441843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1441797#post1441797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, I think the visual novels and LA By Night show that the simplifications of V5 for televison and mass media are very easily incorporated:<br /> <br /> * Vampires have a Masquerade because humans are hunting them and have assault rifles<br /> * Anarchs oppose the Camarilla<br /> * The Tremere are a bunch of feuding wizard houses.<br /> * Neonate vampires are important enough to effect things<br /> <br /> Really, it seems V5 was made to make the gameworld very easy to understand.</div> </div> </div> </div>I totally agree with the last paragraph.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-29T00:12:51-07:00","id":1441864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1441797#post1441797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really, it seems V5 was made to make the gameworld very easy to understand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Strongly disagree. Actually, you're close to being objectively wrong. <br /> <br /> Gangrel/Brujah were simpler than Banu Haquim and Lasombra<br /> Followers of Set were simpler than Ministry/Church. <br /> Giovanni are simpler than the Hecata.<br /> One Tremere were simpler to understand than four. <br /> Why Justify the convoluted SI when you can just use the easier to accept/way cooler SoL/SAD<br /> The Camarilla Et Al is easier to understand than Big Anarchs Vs The Cam... It also means the emphasis is on internal politics rather than external sectarian war which is what you want. <br /> Sabbat in Miami is easier to chew on than Sabbat in Syria. <br /> V5 disciplines are far more difficult to understand than V20 disciplines; Why do two masters of Potence have entirely different abilities? <br /> Thin bloods are way, way, way simpler pre-v5. <br /> <br /> [quote]<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">* Neonate vampires are important enough to effect things</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> They were always important enough to effect things, you just needed to work for it; it wasn't handed to you on a silver plater by all the elders leaving at once. Jyhad means struggle, it's the main hook of vampire; it's not supposed to be easy. &quot;The Prince and primogen all died on holiday, so we're in charge now&quot; makes for a great couple of episodes, but it would be difficult to make a long running series out of it. </span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-29T03:25:41-07:00","id":1441868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1441864#post1441864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V5 disciplines are far more difficult to understand than V20 disciplines; Why do two masters of Potence have entirely different abilities?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually one of the major pros V5 had when I was thinking to move from 20th to it. I love that disciplines have more powers. Though I do think that maybe it should've worked differently. But, it's a subject for a different thread I guess.<br /> <br /> To the topic though, I really can't see how V5 is more complicated. If you only read Revised/20th book and then go to Beckett's Jyhad diary good luck understand all of the metaplot hooks and threads. I really don't like this method of storytelling through products, and the revised/20th really became crazy at some point.<br /> <br /> Also, it seems that people have very strong opinions about clans, and how they *should be* or how they *are*. And I am quite sure that at each gaming table the clans are different. Everyone had a different experience from the game while playing, and every person and ST translate and understand the clans and the lore differently. I don't think anyone is playing the game and the lore as written, without change or personal interpretation. So to me, how the Followers of Set are or the Tremere, or any other aspect of the game, is kinda personal. In Jim's game, they are one thing, and at my table, they are something else. The good thing about V5 is that we really don't have a lot of restricting information, we have enough to build our own world, and I really prefer it that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24461,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24461-godforsaken","user":"Godforsaken","date":". 03-29-2021, 06:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24461-godforsaken","name":"Godforsaken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24461_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-29T03:46:17-07:00","id":1441870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1441781#post1441781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the Crusades AC was the worst of the series, though. Besides, neither order has any similarity to their historical counterparts.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have diffrent tastes than me I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26433-ascentionthemage","name":"AscentionTheMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26433_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-29T04:15:36-07:00","id":1441876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AscentionTheMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1441870#post1441870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You have diffrent tastes than me I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking as a former history teacher, I'd rather present something as a fantasy than attempt to present it as history with elements that can be incredibly misleading. For example, AC: Valhalla as a video game has the monastaries guarded by soldiers because they don't want to portray the Vikings as massacring unarmed defenseless men in order to rob them. Thus they are doing something that whitewashes crimes of history.<br /> <br /> Similarly, in order to present the Spartans as 300 level badasses, they ignore the atrocities and horrors inflicted on the Helots in Odyssey.<br /> <br /> Similarly still, you can play Origins almost entirely without mentioning slavery despite its claims to historical accuracy.<br /> <br /> Why? Because they're worried that Bayak thinking slavery is perfectly normal would....make him unlikable.<br /> <br /> I'd rather have a VAMPIRE: THE DARK AGES game be more like Castlevania or Underworld III: Rise of the Lycans than present something that will misinform the public. The thing is the latter is inevitable because you cannot present vampires in the Middle Ages, the Omen Wars, the monster-hunting Inquisition, and so on without warping history. Because there were no vampires in the Dark Ages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-29T04:46:56-07:00","id":1441880,"title":"","content":"Many interesting topics and opinions!<br /> <br /> My take:<ul><li>It is not a problem at all to have anti-heroes or villains as main protagonists. Troublesome complex characters are always great. GoT has them, as well as Vikings, Black Sails, etc. The Boys is also a great example. usually the trick is that those characters are relatively complex and believe they are doing the right thing.</li> <li>The Elric effect may work in favor or against depending on how it is done. People know all about vampires being both romantic anti-heroes and terrible monsters, one just has to play with expectations and revearsals</li> <li>Totally agree with not shoving up all the lore upfront the viewers but unveiling progressively the different layers. The tone, either horror, parody or soap opera, could vary.</li> <li>Most shows have different storylines that may cross or not, sometimes being related by theme. David Simon is a great example of that with The Wire, The Deuce... I like the idea of first focusing on a single character and then slowly expanding.</li> </ul>And since there are some proposals already, although quite typical, why not mine:<ul><li>The show starts with hunters. The &quot;domestic terrorist&quot; ones that may have gotten involved by revenge or family tradition but totally see themselves as the good guys. They are investigating the horrendous deaths of a serial killer.</li> <li>We learn of the protagonist, the killer: a fledgling who doesn't know s***t about vampires, just that since that horrible thing happened they've got an aversion to light/sunlight/fire plus constant blackouts (frenzies) after which they wake up covered in blood, pretty much like in Dark City, and are totally scared.</li> <li>Something else than the hunters we've learned of, something supernatural and scary, is hunting not just him but has gone after their family and loved ones. Namely, the sheriff, through who we start learning about the vampire Camarilla society, although at this point for the viewer no sects are mentioned. I'd like a Sherliff like Qadir, though and scary but showing that complexity.</li> <li>The hunters start to learn about some interference from Men in Black in cahoots of Priests that threaten them to get out of the way</li> </ul>And so on... It can have some Personal Horror, some Dark Parody of the current world... and all characters should be both likable and doing horrible things to each other. In the end they are all Monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17974-strangelove","name":"Strangelove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17974_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-29T04:54:03-07:00","id":1441881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1441876#post1441876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Similarly, in order to present the Spartans as 300 level badasses, they ignore the atrocities and horrors inflicted on the Helots in Odyssey.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>AC Odyssee was inacurate as fuck: <a href=\"https://youtu.be/KheW7q-Bygg\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/KheW7q-Bygg</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26433-ascentionthemage","name":"AscentionTheMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26433_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-29T06:27:05-07:00","id":1441888,"title":"","content":"I think Ubisoft completely abandoned any notion of accuracy for Origins where you're dark-soulsing giant bosses. Still, <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1441876#post1441876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why? Because they're worried that Bayak thinking slavery is perfectly normal would....make him unlikable.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ah, but you see, Vampires aren't meant to be likeable. Not so much a problem now is it? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd rather have a VAMPIRE: THE DARK AGES game be more like Castlevania or Underworld III: Rise of the Lycans than present something that will misinform the public. The thing is the latter is inevitable because you cannot present vampires in the Middle Ages, the Omen Wars, the monster-hunting Inquisition, and so on without warping history. Because there were no vampires in the Dark Ages. </div> </div> </div>You sure? Along with practices to stop corpses from rising, there are real records of a few people getting killed for Vampirism, with a few werewolves there too. Maybe some of those burnt witches were legit? <br /> <br /> Vampires are few and their impact is negotiable. A good chunk of, say, the omen war can be hidden within mortal skirmishes, crime, banditry, disease or whatever. Such things were extroadinarily common during the period. You don't need Etrius to personally command the invasions of Poland.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-29T06:34:17-07:00","id":1441894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1441888#post1441888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires are few and their impact is negotiable. A good chunk of, say, the omen war can be hidden within mortal skirmishes, crime, banditry, disease or whatever. Such things were extroadinarily common during the period. You don't need Etrius to personally command the invasions of Poland.</div> </div> </div> </div>My ideal Dark Ages series is REDEMPTION based where towns are under siege by hordes of Tzimisce monsters, the Methuselahs live opening in castles with entire regions under their sway, and armies of Tremere minions fight Tzimisce abominations.<br /> <br /> The Masquerade is a nussiance almost no one bothers with.<br /> <br /> The Mythic Age runs wild!<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And yes, you can do it exactly the opposite of this way. However, I think I found it an interesting contrast to the Modern Era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-29T08:06:56-07:00","id":1441910,"title":"","content":"I understand the desire for contrast, but I would prefer to leave the bombastic high-fantasy stuff to older eras, not the medieval. The Methuselah living in temples and proclaiming to be gods (but not being the active rulers, since, y'know, they're only up for the 8 hours everyone else is sleeping.) Maybe up to the migration period.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-29T13:59:33-07:00","id":1441947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1441864#post1441864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strongly disagree. Actually, you're close to being objectively wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to say that's my feeling towards the majority of your posts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Gangrel/Brujah were simpler than Banu Haquim and Lasombra </div> </div> </div>The Rebellious antisocial clans are part of the the Ivory Tower vs... the Anarchs or the Sabbat? The Tzim and Lasombra being the focal point of the &quot;Rebellion&quot; made sense only in the &quot;We are going to make our own sect with Hookers and booze...&quot;<br /> <br /> The brujah and Gangrel being primarily Anarchs makes more sense.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Followers of Set were simpler than Ministry/Church. </div> </div> </div>No, just no. Vampires who focus on religion as a power is pretty simple. vs Settites who are if not taken as &quot;these are D&amp;D larping vampires&quot; requires heavy explanation about aeons and masks of set and and o and so forth.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Giovanni are simpler than the Hecata. </div> </div> </div>Apples and Gala Apples. And even that's debatable with all the minor families and bullshit the Giovanni had. But the Hecata are easier to Understand than Giovanni, Harbingers, Nagaraja, Samedi, Mwlawata(sp)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One Tremere were simpler to understand than four. </div> </div> </div>The first thing I'd say says this post isn't objectively wrong. However I don't think the 4 tremere is really all that complicated.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why Justify the convoluted SI when you can just use the easier to accept/way cooler SoL/SAD </div> </div> </div>You seem to think this is an Either Or situation. SAD and SoL were the build up. The SI is SAD and the SoL with actual resources rather than being &quot;crazy Fox Mulder believes in Vampires..&quot; they are the obvious metaplot evolution <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Camarilla Et Al is easier to understand than Big Anarchs Vs The Cam... It also means the emphasis is on internal politics rather than external sectarian war which is what you want </div> </div> </div>Eat the Rich has been a core theme from 1e onward. the Anarchs have a book in v20. The Cam and Sabbat do not. The Generation war is right there and one that's EASY for people to grasp especially in today's market. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> .<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sabbat in Miami is easier to chew on than Sabbat in Syria. </div> </div> </div>YOU JUST said external sect war is bad So shouldn't putting the Sabbat on teh Bus be a benefit... oh wait that would require you to argue something consistantly other than &quot;I HATE ChANGE&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> V5 disciplines are far more difficult to understand than V20 disciplines; Why do two masters of Potence have entirely different abilities? </div> </div> </div>Why should two masters of a sword have completely different abilities? why should people with Blood magic get to choose a dozen or more in clan disciplines while there's NO variations on super strength....<br /> <br /> Oh.. wait combo disciplines existed.... <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thin bloods are way, way, way simpler pre-v5. </div> </div> </div>You know what they say about stopped clocks...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> [/QUOTE]<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-29T14:41:41-07:00","id":1441954,"title":"","content":"Settites don't really require anymore explanation than Thulsa Doom's cult did in Conan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-29T14:44:47-07:00","id":1441955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1441954#post1441954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Settites don't really require anymore explanation than Thulsa Doom's cult did in Conan.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that....and I hate to say it, Setites often come off as....<br /> <br /> Silly.<br /> <br /> &quot;vampires believe in Caine except these guys who believe in a 5000 year old Egyptian God of Darkness, which the actual mythological figure wasn't, but they do.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-30T01:19:53-07:00","id":1442014,"title":"","content":"Settites are more &quot;A cult which believes reality is a cruel illusion brought about by a malevolent god, and who thus seeks to end this illusion by collective realization (IE reality is so shit it can't be real) <br /> <br /> Also their Messiah was a sexy egyptian stormgod who became best buds with a snake. <br /> <br /> It's very easy to explain if you just grasp the fundamentals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-30T03:22:15-07:00","id":1442021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1442014#post1442014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Settites are more &quot;A cult which believes reality is a cruel illusion brought about by a malevolent god, and who thus seeks to end this illusion by collective realization (IE reality is so shit it can't be real)<br /> <br /> Also their Messiah was a sexy egyptian stormgod who became best buds with a snake.<br /> <br /> It's very easy to explain if you just grasp the fundamentals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your definition of easy includes introducing an entirely new contradictory religion to Kindred that worships evil and contradicts the primary religious narrative/origin. You can do it but I think it is definitely very complex for a TV audience versus the Ministry.<br /> <br /> So YMMV on that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-30T03:37:03-07:00","id":1442022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1441947#post1441947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have to say that's my feeling towards the majority of your posts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, yes. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Rebellious antisocial clans are part of the the Ivory Tower vs... the Anarchs or the Sabbat? The Tzim and Lasombra being the focal point of the &quot;Rebellion&quot; made sense only in the &quot;We are going to make our own sect with Hookers and booze...&quot;<br /> <br /> The brujah and Gangrel being primarily Anarchs makes more sense. </div> </div> </div>The Brujah would never leave wholesale, because they're a clan of individuals with very different opinions from one another and nobody has the right to speak for all of them. Thus they can never collectively decide to 'leave the cam' and abandon representation. You should also remember that a good chunk of brujah are going to have pro-authoritarian, elitist or pragmatic views, or they're otherwise going to support the status quo and order of the Camarilla because nothing's more rebelious than becoming the man/they're intellectually inclined/they're actually older than a hundred. The Lasombra replacement is contrived and difficult for people to understand.<br /> The Gangrel? Sure. Most Gangrel rebellion falls in the domain of autuarks rather than anarchs, however. But this is a Revised edition point, not a V5 one. I don't mind the Assamites replacing them, but I don't like the Banu Haquim updates. In any case, for an audience of laymen, it'd probably be better to be introduced to the Gangrel before the Assamites.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Apples and Gala Apples. And even that's debatable with all the minor families and bullshit the Giovanni had. But the Hecata are easier to Understand than Giovanni, Harbingers, Nagaraja, Samedi, Mwlawata(sp) </div> </div> </div>Those bloodlines are rare as fuck, and honestly work well for a monster-of-the week kinda thing if we're talking a television show. The Giovanni playing game-of-incestuous-thrones with themselves is a strength to be capitalized on. The hecata's just a contrived mess.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The first thing I'd say says this post isn't objectively wrong. However I don't think the 4 tremere is really all that complicated. </div> </div> </div>But considerably less impressive and impactful than THE PYRAMID. Ok, yes, that's very subjective. but do you honesetly believe there are only 4 houses, or that all four houses aren't really masks for some complicated Tremere plot?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You seem to think this is an Either Or situation. SAD and SoL were the build up. The SI is SAD and the SoL with actual resources rather than being &quot;crazy Fox Mulder believes in Vampires..&quot; they are the obvious metaplot evolution </div> </div> </div>Obvious shouldn't refer to &quot;secret segments of different inteligence organizations making secret contact with eachother and a few equally paranoid terrorist groups in order to destroy the vampires that probably control who leads said inteligence organizations and their funding&quot;<br /> -<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Eat the Rich has been a core theme from 1e onward. the Anarchs have a book in v20. The Cam and Sabbat do not. The Generation war is right there and one that's EASY for people to grasp especially in today's market. </div> </div> </div>Generational war doesn't necessarily mean sectarian war, and you're dumbing it down by dividing everything along two lines.<br /> <br /> <br /> .<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> YOU JUST said external sect war is bad So shouldn't putting the Sabbat on teh Bus be a benefit... oh wait that would require you to argue something consistantly other than &quot;I HATE ChANGE&quot; </div> </div> </div>Sabbat have interesting internal conflicts and marvelous politics. You can't have all that when they're offering themselves to a Damascan methuselah by the crateload.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why should two masters of a sword have completely different abilities? </div> </div> </div> Are you taking my side here?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> why should people with Blood magic get to choose a dozen or more in clan disciplines while there's NO variations on super strength.... </div> </div> </div>Imagine being mad at brains for doing so many different things whilst muscles remain simple organs. I'd also argue you can actually do MORE with Classic potence's +Strength than you could with the overly specific V5 disciplines (You can jump real high, but you can't use that strength to kick? What is this? A Garou gift?)<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh.. wait combo disciplines existed.... </div> </div> </div> and they were expensive, few had them, but every single vampire had the capacity to learn them. Very different from the V5 system of everyone having something radically different from their clanmates and all are beholden to a 5 power limit. TV wise, Clans need a visually strong Identity, you can't do that when nobody among a clan exhibits the same powers.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 03-30-2021, 06:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-30T03:40:29-07:00","id":1442023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Generational war doesn't necessarily mean sectarian war, and you're dumbing it down by dividing everything along two lines. </div> </div> </div>Except that there were two sects opposed to one another from the beginning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-30T07:13:25-07:00","id":1442042,"title":"","content":"It's difficult to define Anarchs as a sect. A movement, sure, but not a sect. The Camarilla's a sect. The Sabbat are a Sect. The Settites are a Sect. The Assamites are a sect. The Giovanni... are a Family. But the Anarchs are people with very different ideas from one another, only united by not fitting in with the status quo. The game has never given us the idea that all neonates looking for a leg-up are anarchs, indeed many neonates have always hung to the camarilla clamoring for promotion, and scheming shortcuts for the route.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-30T07:18:51-07:00","id":1442043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1439984-v-tm-netflix-amazon-series?p=1442042#post1442042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's difficult to define Anarchs as a sect. A movement, sure, but not a sect. The Camarilla's a sect. The Sabbat are a Sect. The Settites are a Sect. The Assamites are a sect. The Giovanni... are a Family. But the Anarchs are people with very different ideas from one another, only united by not fitting in with the status quo. The game has never given us the idea that all neonates looking for a leg-up are anarchs, indeed many neonates have always hung to the camarilla clamoring for promotion, and scheming shortcuts for the route.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Anarchs were a sect that merged with the Camarilla and then had several revolts against the Camarilla:<br /> <br /> * The French Revolution<br /> * The Russian Revolution<br /> * The LA Revolution<br /> <br /> Both the Russian Revolution and LA Revolution had territory held by the Brujah Council and the LA Anarchs who existed as seperate from the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> Now in 5th Edition, the Anarchs have fully organized into multiple applied cities that are definitely their own sect.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>."